{"id":"20260827T200632.805285726Z-6dc7e2a2","time":"2026-08-27T20:06:32.805285726Z","session_id":"session-20260827T200002.380147091Z","task_id":"task-1787860802380664460","source":"reviewer","kind":"review.finding","summary":"[f1] blocking: The candidate treats ordinary derived coverage plus prospective coverage as satisfying the new-surface rule. (internal/workflow/engine.go, Engine.derivedCoverage) — The plan requires that a planned file absent at the pinned world be COVERED only by prospective authority. The candidate calls derived.CoveredFiles(anchors, world, planned) before checking whether each planned file exists, and derived.Anchor.Covers only compares its world and listed subject paths; it does not establish that the subject exists in that world. Therefore an anchor that names an absent path can give ordinary derived coverage to a new file, bypassing declaration, closed-role, package, dependency, and post-creation checks. This violates the supplied plan’s ‘absence is not safety’ law. Sensei’s authoritative preflight identifies engine.go as architecture-sensitive and anchors the critical workflow authority invariants; this is an authority bypass, not a test-only defect. → Verify planned-file existence at the pinned world first. Normal derived coverage must be restricted to verified-existing planned paths. Evaluate verified-absent paths only through prospectiveAnchors, and leave errors or undeclared files uncovered.","payload":{"id":"f1","severity":"blocking","claim":"The candidate treats ordinary derived coverage plus prospective coverage as satisfying the new-surface rule.","reference":"internal/workflow/engine.go, Engine.derivedCoverage","reason":"The plan requires that a planned file absent at the pinned world be COVERED only by prospective authority. The candidate calls derived.CoveredFiles(anchors, world, planned) before checking whether each planned file exists, and derived.Anchor.Covers only compares its world and listed subject paths; it does not establish that the subject exists in that world. Therefore an anchor that names an absent path can give ordinary derived coverage to a new file, bypassing declaration, closed-role, package, dependency, and post-creation checks. This violates the supplied plan’s ‘absence is not safety’ law. Sensei’s authoritative preflight identifies engine.go as architecture-sensitive and anchors the critical workflow authority invariants; this is an authority bypass, not a test-only defect.","correction":"Verify planned-file existence at the pinned world first. Normal derived coverage must be restricted to verified-existing planned paths. Evaluate verified-absent paths only through prospectiveAnchors, and leave errors or undeclared files uncovered.","proof_gap":"prospective_test.go tests the helper predicate but does not prove the Engine routing path rejects ordinary derived coverage for an absent file."}}
{"id":"20260827T200632.805428272Z-2043a1b8","time":"2026-08-27T20:06:32.805428272Z","session_id":"session-20260827T200002.380147091Z","task_id":"task-1787860802380664460","source":"reviewer","kind":"review.completed","summary":"REVISE: REVISE: the candidate implements the prospective predicate, but it does not enforce the plan’s exclusive rule that a file absent at the pinned world may be covered only by prospective authority. Sensei’s current authoritative preflight marks this architecture-sensitive and requires preserving workflow authority boundaries.  (reviewer · via codex · session fresh · candidate 6bbbdb4c21d4)","payload":{"provenance":{"task_id":"task-1787860802380664460","role":"reviewer","provider":"codex","session_id":"session-20260827T200002.380147091Z","session_mode":"fresh","base_sha":"29322a2265d2fe266b3bdf75d1ff1d03a7d59e39","candidate_digest":"6bbbdb4c21d486ef","graph_build_commit":"fac399f8225f","at":"2026-08-27T20:06:32.805270397Z"},"decision":"revise","summary":"REVISE: the candidate implements the prospective predicate, but it does not enforce the plan’s exclusive rule that a file absent at the pinned world may be covered only by prospective authority. Sensei’s current authoritative preflight marks this architecture-sensitive and requires preserving workflow authority boundaries.","instructions":"In internal/workflow/engine.go, partition planned files by verified existence at the pinned world before normal derived coverage is computed. Pass only files proven to exist at that world to derived.CoveredFiles; pass absent files solely to prospectiveAnchors. Treat an inability to establish existence as uncovered. Add an engine-level falsifier proving a derived Anchor whose subject list names an absent planned path cannot cover that path without an admissible prospective declaration.","findings":[{"id":"f1","severity":"blocking","claim":"The candidate treats ordinary derived coverage plus prospective coverage as satisfying the new-surface rule.","reference":"internal/workflow/engine.go, Engine.derivedCoverage","reason":"The plan requires that a planned file absent at the pinned world be COVERED only by prospective authority. The candidate calls derived.CoveredFiles(anchors, world, planned) before checking whether each planned file exists, and derived.Anchor.Covers only compares its world and listed subject paths; it does not establish that the subject exists in that world. Therefore an anchor that names an absent path can give ordinary derived coverage to a new file, bypassing declaration, closed-role, package, dependency, and post-creation checks. This violates the supplied plan’s ‘absence is not safety’ law. Sensei’s authoritative preflight identifies engine.go as architecture-sensitive and anchors the critical workflow authority invariants; this is an authority bypass, not a test-only defect.","correction":"Verify planned-file existence at the pinned world first. Normal derived coverage must be restricted to verified-existing planned paths. Evaluate verified-absent paths only through prospectiveAnchors, and leave errors or undeclared files uncovered.","proof_gap":"prospective_test.go tests the helper predicate but does not prove the Engine routing path rejects ordinary derived coverage for an absent file."}]}}
