{"id":"20260827T201008.699565402Z-f63967dd","time":"2026-08-27T20:10:08.699565402Z","session_id":"session-20260827T200002.380147091Z","task_id":"task-1787860802380664460","source":"reviewer","kind":"agent.finished","summary":"Codex finished"}
{"id":"20260827T201008.699730894Z-ef82e5a3","time":"2026-08-27T20:10:08.699730894Z","session_id":"session-20260827T200002.380147091Z","task_id":"task-1787860802380664460","source":"reviewer","kind":"review.finding","summary":"[f1] blocking: A failed read of F is treated as proof that F is absent and may therefore receive prospective authority. (internal/workflow/engine.go:coverPlannedAtWorld and internal/workflow/prospective.go:prospectiveAnchors) — coverPlannedAtWorld partitions every read error into `absent`, then prospectiveAnchors also accepts any read error for F as a create. Thus a transient Git/read failure for F, while S remains readable, can satisfy the remaining clauses and produce a PROSPECTIVE anchor without establishing that F did not exist at the pinned world. The supplied plan permits this path only for a file that does not exist at that world. Sensei's authoritative briefing for prospective.go states the critical principle “meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected”; an unclassified read failure is not absence. → Represent present, confirmed-missing, and unreadable separately. Send only confirmed-missing files to prospectiveAnchors; unreadable files must remain uncovered or make routing fail closed. Preserve this distinction through the Git reader rather than collapsing all errors into absence.","payload":{"id":"f1","severity":"blocking","claim":"A failed read of F is treated as proof that F is absent and may therefore receive prospective authority.","reference":"internal/workflow/engine.go:coverPlannedAtWorld and internal/workflow/prospective.go:prospectiveAnchors","reason":"coverPlannedAtWorld partitions every read error into `absent`, then prospectiveAnchors also accepts any read error for F as a create. Thus a transient Git/read failure for F, while S remains readable, can satisfy the remaining clauses and produce a PROSPECTIVE anchor without establishing that F did not exist at the pinned world. The supplied plan permits this path only for a file that does not exist at that world. Sensei's authoritative briefing for prospective.go states the critical principle “meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected”; an unclassified read failure is not absence.","correction":"Represent present, confirmed-missing, and unreadable separately. Send only confirmed-missing files to prospectiveAnchors; unreadable files must remain uncovered or make routing fail closed. Preserve this distinction through the Git reader rather than collapsing all errors into absence.","proof_gap":"The dark-world test makes both S and F unreadable, so it cannot expose the case where S is readable, F is unreadable, and an inadmissible prospective grant is issued."}}
{"id":"20260827T201008.699775679Z-fac6cbc3","time":"2026-08-27T20:10:08.699775679Z","session_id":"session-20260827T200002.380147091Z","task_id":"task-1787860802380664460","source":"reviewer","kind":"review.finding","summary":"[f2] blocking: Post-creation inspection checks the same authorization facts that routing read. (internal/workflow/engine.go:Engine.prospective, setProspectiveGrants, prospectiveGrants, runCandidate, and Resume) — The grant facts exist only in the in-memory `Engine.prospective` map. Resume restores the declaration into taskContext but does not restore/recompute the corresponding grants or facts. After process restart or resume, inspection receives an empty facts map and no longer checks against S's pinned-world imports; it can either falsely refute a valid test importing an S import or accept an allowance-only shape without the original authorization record. This conflicts with the plan's requirement that inspection use the same facts that authorized creation. Sensei's briefing for engine.go identifies the workflow's execution and task-state boundaries as critical. → Store the immutable prospective authorization receipt/grants with the resumable task bound, including S, world identity, package, and import set; restore it before runCandidate. Alternatively, recompute it from the persisted pinned world and persisted routing anchors, failing closed if exact re-establishment is impossible.","payload":{"id":"f2","severity":"blocking","claim":"Post-creation inspection checks the same authorization facts that routing read.","reference":"internal/workflow/engine.go:Engine.prospective, setProspectiveGrants, prospectiveGrants, runCandidate, and Resume","reason":"The grant facts exist only in the in-memory `Engine.prospective` map. Resume restores the declaration into taskContext but does not restore/recompute the corresponding grants or facts. After process restart or resume, inspection receives an empty facts map and no longer checks against S's pinned-world imports; it can either falsely refute a valid test importing an S import or accept an allowance-only shape without the original authorization record. This conflicts with the plan's requirement that inspection use the same facts that authorized creation. Sensei's briefing for engine.go identifies the workflow's execution and task-state boundaries as critical.","correction":"Store the immutable prospective authorization receipt/grants with the resumable task bound, including S, world identity, package, and import set; restore it before runCandidate. Alternatively, recompute it from the persisted pinned world and persisted routing anchors, failing closed if exact re-establishment is impossible.","proof_gap":"No test interrupts and resumes a task containing a prospective declaration, then verifies both accepted S imports and rejection of imports outside S plus the role allowance."}}
{"id":"20260827T201008.699859618Z-c99993b0","time":"2026-08-27T20:10:08.699859618Z","session_id":"session-20260827T200002.380147091Z","task_id":"task-1787860802380664460","source":"reviewer","kind":"review.completed","summary":"REVISE: The candidate implements most of the predicate, but it can grant prospective coverage when F's existence at the pinned world is unknown, and it loses the authorization facts across resume. Both violate the closed, pinned-world authority boundary. Sensei is authoritative/current and its briefing applies the critical principle “meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected.”  (reviewer · via codex · session fresh · candidate 98524291c9e0)","payload":{"provenance":{"task_id":"task-1787860802380664460","role":"reviewer","provider":"codex","session_id":"session-20260827T200002.380147091Z","session_mode":"fresh","base_sha":"29322a2265d2fe266b3bdf75d1ff1d03a7d59e39","candidate_digest":"98524291c9e0dc70","graph_build_commit":"fac399f8225f","at":"2026-08-27T20:10:08.699718561Z"},"decision":"revise","summary":"The candidate implements most of the predicate, but it can grant prospective coverage when F's existence at the pinned world is unknown, and it loses the authorization facts across resume. Both violate the closed, pinned-world authority boundary. Sensei is authoritative/current and its briefing applies the critical principle “meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected.”","instructions":"Make pinned-world existence tri-state: only a positively established missing path may enter prospective authorization; unreadable/failed reads must leave the file uncovered or fail the route. Persist the exact prospective grants (declared path, covering S, pinned-world package/import facts, and world identity) in task/session-bound state, restore them on Resume, and inspect against those restored facts. Add focused tests for an unreadable F with readable S and for interrupted/resumed prospective inspection.","findings":[{"id":"f1","severity":"blocking","claim":"A failed read of F is treated as proof that F is absent and may therefore receive prospective authority.","reference":"internal/workflow/engine.go:coverPlannedAtWorld and internal/workflow/prospective.go:prospectiveAnchors","reason":"coverPlannedAtWorld partitions every read error into `absent`, then prospectiveAnchors also accepts any read error for F as a create. Thus a transient Git/read failure for F, while S remains readable, can satisfy the remaining clauses and produce a PROSPECTIVE anchor without establishing that F did not exist at the pinned world. The supplied plan permits this path only for a file that does not exist at that world. Sensei's authoritative briefing for prospective.go states the critical principle “meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected”; an unclassified read failure is not absence.","correction":"Represent present, confirmed-missing, and unreadable separately. Send only confirmed-missing files to prospectiveAnchors; unreadable files must remain uncovered or make routing fail closed. Preserve this distinction through the Git reader rather than collapsing all errors into absence.","proof_gap":"The dark-world test makes both S and F unreadable, so it cannot expose the case where S is readable, F is unreadable, and an inadmissible prospective grant is issued."},{"id":"f2","severity":"blocking","claim":"Post-creation inspection checks the same authorization facts that routing read.","reference":"internal/workflow/engine.go:Engine.prospective, setProspectiveGrants, prospectiveGrants, runCandidate, and Resume","reason":"The grant facts exist only in the in-memory `Engine.prospective` map. Resume restores the declaration into taskContext but does not restore/recompute the corresponding grants or facts. After process restart or resume, inspection receives an empty facts map and no longer checks against S's pinned-world imports; it can either falsely refute a valid test importing an S import or accept an allowance-only shape without the original authorization record. This conflicts with the plan's requirement that inspection use the same facts that authorized creation. Sensei's briefing for engine.go identifies the workflow's execution and task-state boundaries as critical.","correction":"Store the immutable prospective authorization receipt/grants with the resumable task bound, including S, world identity, package, and import set; restore it before runCandidate. Alternatively, recompute it from the persisted pinned world and persisted routing anchors, failing closed if exact re-establishment is impossible.","proof_gap":"No test interrupts and resumes a task containing a prospective declaration, then verifies both accepted S imports and rejection of imports outside S plus the role allowance."}]}}
